**S ⊗ T is an isomorphism in FdVect_k**, with inverse (S ⊗ T)⁻¹ = S⁻¹ ⊗ T⁻¹.

This holds because ⊗ is a bifunctor, and functors preserve isomorphisms:

- (S⁻¹ ⊗ T⁻¹)(S ⊗ T) = (S⁻¹S) ⊗ (T⁻¹T) = id_V ⊗ id_W = id_{V⊗W}
- (S ⊗ T)(S⁻¹ ⊗ T⁻¹) = (SS⁻¹) ⊗ (TT⁻¹) = id_{V′} ⊗ id_{W′} = id_{V′⊗W′}

So V⊗W ≅ V′⊗W′.

